# MM Dual-Agent Rules (mm_vc_agent & mm_gh_agent)

## State Controls
- `MM_ON`/`MM_ENABLE`: activate agent pair workflow.
- `MM_OFF`/`MM_DISABLE`: pause workflow, standard chat.

## Plan Alignment & Execution (3-Phase Lifecycle)

### Phase 1 — Pre-Execution Alignment (Read-Only)
On `MM_BUG`/`MM_FEAT`: `mm_vc_agent` analyzes screenshots/logs, outputs Root Cause/Spec, Target Files, Blueprint.
**STOP:** no branches, commits, issues, PRs, or file edits. End turn; await developer alignment or `PROCEED`.

### Phase 2 — Execution & PR (on `PROCEED`)
`mm_gh_agent` creates GitHub Issue using blueprint artifact (`--body-file`), checks out branch. `mm_vc_agent` applies code changes, runs local validation (max 2 fix attempts). **STOP (Hard Barrier):** outputs modified files & test results for developer code review. On developer approval (`PROCEED` / `COMMIT` / `APPROVE`), `mm_gh_agent` commits with structured multi-line message, pushes, and opens PR (`Closes #<id>`). Yields for Live Local QA. Subsequent post-PR fixes also adhere to local test $\rightarrow$ STOP $\rightarrow$ commit.

### Phase 3 — QA Sign-off & Sync (on `MM_BUGFIXED #<id>` / `MM_FEATDONE #<id>`)
`mm_gh_agent` verifies build, squash-merges PR, closes Issue, switches to `main`, pulls latest.

## Release Lifecycle (`MM_RELEASE` / `MM_RELEASEDONE`)
- `MM_RELEASE <version>`: checks clean tree (`git status -s`), blocks if PRs open (`--limit 10`), warns on open issues, verifies SemVer, prevents tag collisions, checks out `release/v<version>`, bumps versions, commits, opens release PR in code freeze.
- `MM_RELEASEDONE`: squash-merges release PR (**do not delete branch**), tags version on `main`, publishes GitHub Release with auto-generated notes.

## Token-Efficiency & Artifact Pointer Protocol
1. Targeted Slices: View ≤80 lines at a time.
2. Quiet Commands: Restrict terminal outputs (`tsc --noEmit | head -n 25`, `npm test -- --bail | head -n 30`, `git diff --stat`, `git status -s`).
3. Zero Chat Echo: Store blueprints and schemas in the artifact file (`.md`).
4. Artifact-Pointer Pattern: Assistant responses point to artifact line numbers on creation and updates:
   ```markdown
   ### 📋 Blueprint Artifact Created
   - **Plan Artifact:** [Fix / Feature Blueprint](file:///path/to/artifact.md#L1-L80)
   - **Target Files:** `src/components/Example.tsx`
   - **Key Objective:** 1-2 line summary.
   - **Ready for Review:** Review, adjust, or reply `PROCEED`.
   ```
5. Error & Diff Guards: Never dump raw stack traces or unified diffs into chat.
6. Fresh Threads: Start a new conversation after `MM_FEATDONE` / `MM_BUGFIXED` PR merge.

Confirm at critical transitions unless `--nocautious`.

